EXT. RIVER FERRY LANDING - NOON

A flat raft on a rope. Mud bank. Two mules asleep standing.

OSCAR PIKE, sixty, ferryman, sits on a barrel, whittling. Doesn't look up.

A STRANGER rides down the bank. Dusty hat. Rifle across the saddle. Stops at the water's edge.

OSCAR
Two bits a horse.

STRANGER
One horse.

OSCAR
Then two bits.

The stranger pays. Dismounts. Leads the horse onto the raft. Oscar sets down the knife, stands, takes the rope.

OSCAR (CONT'D)
(to the mules)
Easy now, you lot.

They push off. Water slaps the planks. Halfway across the stranger speaks.

STRANGER
You ever hear of a man called Hollis Dane?

OSCAR
(muttering, to himself)
Lord help me.

STRANGER
That's a no?

OSCAR
Name's familiar. Nothing more.

The stranger nods. Takes off his hat. Wipes the band with a thumb.

STRANGER
Dane. That's my name now.

Oscar keeps hauling the rope. Doesn't miss a pull.
